{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792308374,"nonce":"t5RZD1/Z2XJjxFxiFkSGzq1JMLE=","title":"blinc_gpu: close the gap between GpuPrimitive and the blinc_abi display list","message":"Decision (owner, 2026-10-18): GpuPrimitive and blinc_gpu catch up with what ashui and blinc_ts already draw, whatever the DSL does. The ABI records (DISPLAY_LIST_VERSION 1, 112 floats) are the pixel contract for scenes that come from the ABI; Blinc-native trees keep their path. This settles decision 3 in 5e711e5 and makes its option R1 the plan. Facts marked read come from source, not from a run.\n\n\nReference consumers\n\nblinc_ts draws records with six pipelines (box, shadow, backdrop, layer, text, image; about 2.7k lines of generated WGSL from about 1.2k lines of TypeScript). ashui's are ports of Blinc's sdf_core and sdf_shadow. blinc_gpu has sdf_core, sdf_shadow, sdf_notch, sdf_3d, glass and text, each with a storage-buffer, vertex-buffer and data-texture form; the latter two are generated into OUT_DIR from the base shader.\n\n\nRecord to GpuPrimitive, by row (read)\n\nMaps field for field: bounds, corner radii, fill, gradient end, border colour, shadow and its colour, clip bounds and radii, gradient params, corner shape n, primitive and fill type. The 2D transform is a general 2x2 plus origin in the record, rotation sin/cos plus local_affine in GpuPrimitive, so it needs a conversion, not a copy.\n\nMissing in Blinc:\n- per-side border colours (rows 16 to 19). Blinc keeps per-side widths in border[4] and one colour; fill_rect_with_per_side_border takes one colour.\n- a local (element-space) clip, the second clip in the record. GpuPrimitive has one clip, in screen space.\n- clip-path in the element's frame (rows 22 to 24): inverse transform plus ellipse, rounded rect or polygon. Blinc's clip-path is screen space.\n- an even-odd fill rule on polygon clips. blinc_gpu's clip uses nonzero winding (open: 178a63b); even-odd exists only for path tessellation behind a debug env var.\n- the on-screen rect of the innermost fading clip (row 20). Blinc has clip_fade distances; whether they mean the same is not checked.\n\nPresent in Blinc, different encoding, to map and compare:\n- multi-stop gradients, spread modes and conic (Blinc has a gradient texture; the record uses a table after the records).\n- layers: group opacity, colour matrix, Gaussian blur, drop shadow (Blinc: push_layer and LayerEffect).\n- backdrop blur, colour filter and the glass rim (Blinc: glass pipelines).\n- notch (Blinc: its own pipeline; blinc_ts folds it into the box shader).\n- text: glyph quads sampling the encoder's own mask and colour atlases, uploaded by revision (read_atlas). blinc_gpu's text pipeline owns its atlas, so it needs an external-atlas binding.\n- images and canvases: renderer-owned slots (PRIM_IMAGE 32, PRIM_CANVAS 33).\n\nResolved by the ABI walk, nothing to do in the GPU: dotted, dashed and double borders are emitted as ordinary records (display_list.rs).\n\nBlinc has and the record does not: 3D SDF (perspective, sdf_3d, light, groups), per-primitive CSS filter rows, mask gradient rows, particles, meshes, flow and custom passes. These stay Blinc-native until the ABI grows rows for them (a version bump); that is a separate question from this issue.\n\n\nShape of the work\n\n1. A record decoder in blinc_gpu: records to GpuPrimitive for the rows that map, behind a version check on DISPLAY_LIST_VERSION and record size, as blinc_ts does when it loads the addon.\n2. Extend GpuPrimitive and the base SDF shaders for the missing rows, one at a time, each with an offscreen test against the ABI's own expectation. Per-side colours and the second clip come first; they are what ordinary CSS boxes use.\n3. External glyph atlas binding, then images and canvases.\n4. Layers and backdrop, mapped onto the existing layer and glass code.\n5. Even-odd clip fill rule, which also closes 178a63b for Blinc-native trees.\n\nOpen: whether to extend GpuPrimitive in place (every pipeline reads it) or add a record-reading pipeline set modelled on blinc_ts's six. In place keeps one SDF implementation; a separate set isolates the ABI path from regressions in Blinc-native painting.\n\nRelated: 5e711e5 (DSL on blinc_abi), 6f7b001 (engine model), 178a63b (clip-path fill rule).","files":null}]}